From: postmarketOS <bramble@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd-mbhc: add ALSA jack controls for the headset jack

MBHC registers the headset jack as an input device only. PulseAudio and
PipeWire follow ALSA jack controls (UCM JackControl), so they could not
switch to headphones on plug-in. Add "Headphone Jack" and "Headset Mic
Jack" controls to the same jack; snd_jack_report() keeps them in sync.

---
--- a/techpack/audio/asoc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.c	2026-10-23 01:17:12.685159767 +0100
+++ b/techpack/audio/asoc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.c	2026-10-23 01:17:12.703864925 +0100
@@ -1846,6 +1846,22 @@
 			return ret;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * The jack above is only an input device. Desktop sound
+		 * servers (PulseAudio, PipeWire) follow ALSA jack controls
+		 * instead, so add "Headphone Jack" and "Headset Mic Jack".
+		 */
+		ret = snd_jack_add_new_kctl(mbhc->headset_jack.jack,
+					    "Headphone", SND_JACK_HEADPHONE);
+		if (ret)
+			pr_err("%s: Failed to add headphone jack kctl\n",
+			       __func__);
+		ret = snd_jack_add_new_kctl(mbhc->headset_jack.jack,
+					    "Headset Mic", SND_JACK_MICROPHONE);
+		if (ret)
+			pr_err("%s: Failed to add headset mic jack kctl\n",
+			       __func__);
+
 		ret = snd_soc_card_jack_new(component->card,
 					    "Button Jack",
 					    WCD_MBHC_JACK_BUTTON_MASK,
